From: fairbird <rrrr53@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: guard memchr re-declaration against glibc 2.43 _Generic

glibc 2.43 declares memchr via _Generic/_Overloadable macros when
_FORTIFY_SOURCE is set. Re-declaring it as a plain extern causes:
  "error: expected identifier or '(' before '_Generic'"

Guard the declaration so it is skipped when memchr is already
provided as a macro by the system headers.
---
 include/l_stdlib.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/l_stdlib.h b/include/l_stdlib.h
--- a/include/l_stdlib.h
+++ b/include/l_stdlib.h
@@ -221,7 +221,9 @@ extern	int	toupper		(int);
 
 #ifndef HAVE_MEMCHR
+#ifndef memchr
 extern void *memchr(const void *s, int c, size_t n);
+#endif
 #endif
 
 #ifndef HAVE_STRNLEN
